      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to understand the geometry of the situation when the square is folded along the lines \\(DE\\) and \\(DF\\). After the fold, sides \\(AD\\) and \\(CD\\) coincide and lie on diagonal \\(BD\\). Let's denote the length of \\(AE\\) and \\(CF\\) as \\(x\\). Then \\(EB = BF = 1 - x\\).\n\nWhen the square is folded, the points \\(A\\), \\(B\\), and \\(C\\) coincide on diagonal \\(BD\\). This means that the distances from \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) to the sides \\(AB\\) and \\(CB\\) are equal to the distances from \\(A\\) and \\(C\\) to the diagonal \\(BD\\), respectively.\n\nWe need to find the length of segment \\(AE\\) such that after folding, \\(AD\\) and \\(CD\\) coincide on diagonal \\(BD\\). This implies that the fold lines \\(DE\\) and \\(DF\\) are symmetric with respect to the line \\(BD\\). The fold line \\(DE\\) is the perpendicular bisector of \\(BE\\), and the fold line \\(DF\\) is the perpendicular bisector of \\(BF\\).\n\nThe coordinates of the points can be set up as follows:\n- \\(A = (0, 1)\\)\n- \\(B = (1, 1)\\)\n- \\(C = (1, 0)\\)\n- \\(D = (0, 0)\\)\n\nAfter folding, the new coordinates of \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) will be \\(D = (0, 0)\\) and the new coordinates of \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) will be symmetric with respect to the line \\(BD\\). The equation of the line \\(BD\\) is \\(y = x\\).\n\nThe fold line \\(DE\\) is the perpendicular bisector of \\(BE\\), and \\(BE\\) is a horizontal line segment. The fold line \\(DF\\) is the perpendicular bisector of \\(BF\\), and \\(BF\\) is also a horizontal line segment. The points \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) are on sides \\(AB\\) and \\(CB\\), respectively, and their coordinates will be such that the fold lines divide the segments \\(AE\\) and \\(CF\\) into equal parts.\n\nThe length of \\(AE\\) is given by \\(\\sqrt{k} - m\\). After folding, the length of \\(AE\\) will be the same as the length of \\(CF\\), which is \\(1 - x\\). The fold lines divide the segments into equal parts, and the distance from \\(A\\) to \\(E\\) (or \\(F\\)) along the fold lines is \\(x\\). The remaining distance from the fold line to the diagonal \\(BD\\) is \\(\\sqrt{m^2} = m\\) units (since the fold line is symmetric and the length of \\(AE\\) is \\(\\sqrt{k} - m\\)).\n\nThe length of \\(AE\\) can be expressed as:\n\\[ AE = 1 - x = \\sqrt{6 - \\sqrt{5}} - 1 \\]\nwhere \\(k = 6\\) and \\(m = 1\\). Therefore, \\(k + m = 5\\).\n\nThe integer value of \\(k + m\\) is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
